# Open per-script questions

Three things I'd push on:

1. **Vale's second "Cut the channel" / Leena's second "Don't"** in scene 1.13. Story has only one such exchange. I added a second after the I-do-not-yet-trust-my-reasons line because Vale's instinct would re-fire after a second shock. _If you'd rather we honor the source's single exchange, delete the second one — the scene still works._
2. **Mira's chair falling.** Story has it; I rendered it as an off-screen sound effect. Alternative: render it visible, with a cut to the chair on the floor. The on-screen version is more cinematic, but it pulls focus from Mira's face. _My instinct: keep it audio-only. The scene is about her face._
3. **The cursor blinking three times before cut to black** (1.15). Three feels right because three is the cadence the audience has learned over the episode. Two would feel rushed; four would feel pretentious. _Producer call._

— End of script V1. Notes welcome. — John
